.TH NEO-REMOTE 1 "2026-11-22" "gnome-phone" "GNOME Phone"
.SH NAME
neo-remote \- infrared remote app for GNOME Phone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neo-remote
.SH DESCRIPTION
Turns the phone's IR LED into a remote. A remote is added by brand (the brand's Power codes are sent one at a time;
the first one the device reacts to keeps that remote with all its buttons), by model from the code database, or empty.
A remote's buttons are a grid: a tap sends, a long press deletes; + adds a button by protocol, address and command or
as raw timings. The record button records a macro from the buttons tapped next (Pause adds a wait); macros run from the
home page, a long press deletes one.
.PP
Everything infrared is the session service org.minerva.Ir1 of Minerva's minerva-ir package (its settings in
.IR ir.conf ).
The app's words, icons and settings are its ui.json.
.SH SEE ALSO
minerva-ir(1), ir-ctl(1)
